# Patterns here are matched against the CONTEXT ROOT and are not recursive on their own,
# so the `**/` forms are what actually keep a nested copy out. That is not theoretical:
# a git worktree under `.claude/worktrees/` carries its own `node_modules` symlink and
# `.next` build, and sent ~500 MB to the daemon on every build until it was named here.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
.git
**/.git

# Tooling scratch: worktrees, session state. Never part of an image.
.claude
